<figure class="card-diagram">
  <div class="card-diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      class="topology"
      viewBox="0 0 820 390"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="ai-workflow-title ai-workflow-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
    >
      <title id="ai-workflow-title">How a task is routed, scoped and closed back into context</title>
      <desc id="ai-workflow-desc">
        A six-step loop. One: the task is classified, which decides which model
        and how much effort it gets before any document loads. Two: a
        hand-written router names the one or two documents the task actually
        needs — contextualization as curation rather than search. Three: the
        work is planned into a short ordered list of phases, with independent
        read-only work sent to a separate sub-agent instead of running in the
        main session. Four: the instruction itself is scoped to a small,
        budgeted change rather than a summary of the whole session. Five: a
        boundary decides what data crosses into the agent or a tool and what
        stays orchestrator-only, the same way a credential can be scoped to
        read without write. Six: once the goal is confirmed, documentation is
        updated, validated and periodically compacted — and that compacted
        state is what the next task's step one reads.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker id="ai-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="arrow-head" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" stroke="none" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="classify" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 1, classify the task and route the model — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="64">1 · Classify &amp; route</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="82">task type decides model</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="98">and effort, before docs load</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M261,82 L287,82" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="context" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 2, contextualize through the router — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="287" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="301" y="64">2 · Contextualize (RAC)</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="82">router names 1–2 docs</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="98">zero repo-wide searches</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M533,82 L559,82" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="plan" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 3, plan goals and phases, delegate to sub-agents — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="559" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="573" y="64">3 · Plan &amp; delegate</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="82">phases before file changes</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="98">read-only work → sub-agent</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M682,124 L682,230" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="scope" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 4, scope the prompt to a token budget — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="559" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="573" y="254">4 · Scope the prompt</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="272">small, budgeted diff</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="288">2–15 net lines typical</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M559,272 L533,272" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="security" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 5, what crosses the boundary and what stays orchestrator-only — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="287" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="301" y="254">5 · Security boundary</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="272">read access to do the task</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="288">not standing write access</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M287,272 L261,272" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="close" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 6, ship, validate and compact — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="254">6 · Ship, validate, compact</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="272">docs replace prose, checked</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="288">compacted for the next task</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link ephemeral-link" d="M138,230 L138,124" marker-end="url(#ai-arrow)" />
      <text class="wire accent" x="150" y="182">feeds the next</text>
      <text class="wire accent" x="150" y="196">task's step 1</text>

      <text class="wire accent" x="15" y="340">1.6k lines across 13 documents</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="358">a common task reads the entry doc plus 1–2 more —</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="374">a stated cost per task, not a hope the context window absorbs it.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="card-diagram-caption">
    Click any step to read what it means.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
